        "reviewer_name": "R. Crowell",
        "review_title": "Product not as described",
        "rating": 1,
        "review_text": "Cable is not SOOW (Service cable, Oil resistant outer, Oil resistant inner, and Weather resistant).  It is 10/3, but it has a thin insulation and sheath, and has a surface that is not smooth as expected but has ribs.  The markings on it are illegible because of the ribs, but does appear to read 300V, not 600V.  This would make it a SJ (Service Junior) prefix.  I put an iron to the end and it melted, so it has an outer sheath that is Thermoplastic (melts in hot environment) which requires a T in its cable type (like STOW or in this case the cable at best is SJTOW Service, Junior, Thermoplastic, Oil resistant outer only maybe, Weather (water & UV?) resistant).  I needed a SOOW, no J, no T, both Os and a W.  This is not it.\nRead more",
